{
  "name": "physics",
  "note": "CMS Phase-2 physics objects (the NanoAOD of Ember's earlier whole-detector export): AK4 Puppi jets (ak4PFJetsPuppi, raw: RECO has no jet energy corrections) as cones from the leading primary vertex to the calorimeter surface (r 129 cm, |z| 320 cm), with their constituents; AK4 CHS jets (ak4PFJetsCHS, the jets the RECO b-tags are computed on: DeepCSV and jet probability), hidden; Puppi MET (pfMetPuppi) and PF MET (pfMet, hidden: at PU200 dominated by pile-up) as arrows; electrons of both Phase-2 chains (barrel gedGsfElectrons, HGCal ecalDrivenGsfElectronsHGC) as helices from their vertex to their supercluster, with GSF track, closest track, supercluster and PF candidate; photons (gedPhotons, photonsHGC) as lines to their supercluster; superclusters with their hits (hidden); hadronic taus (HPS, one per AK4 PF jet: unticked, decay mode required) with their signal candidates; inclusive secondary vertices with their tracks. Jets, MET, photons and taus start at row 0 of the primary vertices (the vertex PUPPI treats as the hard scatter), gathered through relations that are not written. Truth: primary and secondary vertices are matched to truth vertices by CMSSW (pT^2 share of their tracks); jets, MET, e/gamma, taus and superclusters have no associator (truth-graph.md gaps 21-24). Physics domain: shared, the barrel and endcap calorimeter surfaces framed (r 180, |z| 350), 3D, the start domain. Each kind one colour (fixedColour; colourBy none for viewers without it). Muons (muon.json) are declared here too, so they are listed between electrons and photons. Caveat measured on the ttbar samples: PUPPI gives weight 0 to every HGCal (pfTICL) neutral candidate at PU200 and to 94% of HF candidates even at 0PU, so Puppi jets and MET miss neutral energy above |eta| 1.5.",
